From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 02:35:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] radv/ps5: mesh shaders as compute behind
 EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE, and nothing left on the NGG path

Driver patch for EglantinePS5 on Mesa f5610fe2709, after exploitizm's e10371e0d3 and f822c1e9df
(lead-mesh-05, lead-mesh-06) and the stall dump (lead-mesh-01 to 04). Off unless the switches are set.

EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE=1 turns the path on. His build has it on by default; unset here, so a
T42 env behaves as T42. /data/eglantineps5/radv-mesh-compute.txt holding 0 still turns it off.

With the path on, a mesh draw of a pipeline the path refused is dropped and logged. His build leaves
such a pipeline on the NGG mesh path, the one that hangs this GPU, and an Ocarina log has a mesh
program with 4 per-primitive lines, which his limits refuse. Those pipelines ask for no 320 MiB
mesh scratch ring either. Each refusal says why ("mesh shader not run as compute: ...").

The cache's UUID stays as it was: his line changed it for every pipeline, and a cold boot has ended
out of memory on this console (runs 135, 146, 150). The switch goes into the hash of pipelines with
a task shader only.

EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE_MIB=<8 to 512> sizes the buffer (128 unset; it is in the same hash).
EDEN_NX2_RADV_MESH_COMPUTE_PASSES=<n> caps the passes of a chunk: every pass costs its flushes even
when empty, and mesh workgroups past the last pass are left out.

EDEN_NX2_RADV_STALL_DUMP=1 turns the stall dump and the offer of it to the app on. The dump names
the compute pass as "mesh-as-compute".

One fix to his code. In radv_mesh_compute_draw's indirect branch the task pass's own block_va hid the
draw's, so radv_mesh_compute_chunk got the radv_task_emu_block's address, and its compute pass read
records, payload, header and slots from the wrong memory. The inner one is task_block_va now. His
head f822c1e9df has the same line. Our core skips indirect task and mesh draws today, so nothing
reaches this yet.

A refused buffer says so on stderr ("no memory for the mesh compute buffer"): the task pipeline fails
with it, and with EDEN_NX2_PIPELINE_FAIL_SOFT=1 that looks like draws that show nothing.

Not built, not run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
